From 6eb3dca1e7f783a1ba6264a09e6ce6cf875786f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Castro <daniel.castro@tecnico.ulisboa.pt>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 11:25:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] x86 TSX: decoder, instructions, HTM sequencer calibration

Add x86 TSX instruction support (XBEGIN, XEND, XABORT, XTEST):
- New decoder formats in htm.isa
- Instruction implementations in insts/htm.cc and htmruby.cc
- HTM checkpoint save/restore in htm.hh/htm.cc
- Ruby HTM sequencer with calibratable start/commit latencies

Calibration to Broadwell-EP v4 (Xeon E5-2648L v4 @ 1.80 GHz):
- htm_start_latency=60 cycles (XBEGIN cost)
- htm_commit_latency=178 cycles (XEND cost)
- RubyHTMSequencer params in Sequencer.py

Also:
- Set CPUID RTM bit in X86ISA.py
- Add ISA::startup() for HTM checkpoint initialization
- Add build_opts/X86_TSX for TSX + Ruby builds
